  "text": "Please note that the question seems to contain an error, as it asks for the number of positive integers less than 500 that can be expressed as the sum of two distinct perfect squares. However, perfect squares only apply to positive integers, not sums.\n\nTo find the number of positive integers less than 500 that can be expressed as the sum of two distinct perfect squares, we need to consider all the even numbers less than 500 that can be written as the sum of two different squares (like \\(8 = 1^2 + 3^2\\)).\n\nTherefore, we'll iterate over the possible distinct perfect squares and find the even numbers less than 500 that can be expressed in this manner.\n\nLet's write the Python code to find and count such numbers.\n```python\n# Let's find all possible sums of two distinct perfect squares less than 500\r\nperfect_squares = []\r\nsmallest_square = 1\r\nlargest_square = int((500 - 1)**0.5) + 1\r\n\r\n# We'll generate a range of perfect squares from 1^2 to largest...^2\r\nfor i in range(smallest_square, largest_square):\r\n    perfect_squares.append(i * i)\r\n\r\n# We can consider the smallest perfect square of each generated perfect square and greater than itself\r\nperfect_squares_sorted = sorted(perfect_squares)\r\n# Looking for sums of two distinct numbers (of generated perfect squares) that are lower than 500\r\nsums_less_than_500 = []\r\nfor i in range(len(perfect_squares_sorted)):\r\n    for j in range(i + 1, len(perfect_squares_sorted)):\r\n        # Get the sum of the perfect squares\r\n        perfect_squares_sum = perfect_squares_sorted[i] + perfect_squares_sorted[j]\r\n        # Don't add sums that are equal to perfect_squares less than 500\r\n        if perfect_squares_sum < 500:\r\n            sums_less_than_500.append(perfect_squares_sum)\r\n        else:\r\n            break\r\n\r\n# Now we just need to count the sums that are integers less than 500 and greater than 1\r\n# We don't need to filter the sum as already done in the previously.\r\n\r\n# the perfection of the previous sum\r\ncount_of_possible_numbers = len(sums_less_than_500)\r\n\r\n# Final answer\r\nprint(count_of_possible_numbers)\n```\n```output\n122\n```\nThe number of positive integers less than 500 that can be expressed as the sum of two distinct perfect squares is \\(\\boxed{122}\\).",
